{"audit_findings": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "This ontology demonstrates sophisticated structural modeling with proper reification patterns and inverse properties. However, it suffers from critical EDIFACT semantic loss: it models generic segments without qualifier-specific distinctions (NAD+BY vs NAD+SU are indistinguishable), lacks ~60% of mandatory D96A INVOIC segments, and fails to enforce EANCOM cardinality/datatype constraints. The ontology is architecturally sound but semantically incomplete for D96A compliance.",
  "completeness_score": 0.35,
  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "NadBuyerSegment (NAD+BY)",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "D96A EANCOM mandates distinct Buyer identification. Current generic NadSegment cannot enforce that NAD+BY requires either GLN (n13) OR full postal address. Buyer is MANDATORY in EANCOM invoicing."
    },
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name":", "owl_reviewed_length": 22584, "consultation_logged": true, "audits_remaining": 2}

