{"audit_findings": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "This ontology demonstrates a solid structural foundation but suffers from critical D96A EANCOM INVOIC incompleteness. Coverage is approximately 25-30% of required segments. Major gaps include monetary amounts (MOA), quantities (QTY), tax details (TAX), references (RFF), dates with qualifiers (DTM), and line item pricing structures. The qualifier distinction problem is severe - NAD segments lack role-specific subclasses, and date properties are unqualified strings.",
  "completeness_score": 0.28,
  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "MOASegment (Monetary Amount)",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "MANDATORY in D96A EANCOM INVOIC. Required for line item amounts, tax amounts, allowances/charges, and document totals. The ontology currently has :InvoiceAmount and :hasTaxAmount as datatype properties, but MOA segments are complex structures with qualifiers (e.g., MOA+79 for line", "owl_reviewed_length": 14303, "consultation_logged": true, "audits_remaining": 1}

