{"audit_findings": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "This ontology demonstrates sophisticated OWL modeling with proper inverse properties and class hierarchies, but fundamentally fails as a D96A EANCOM INVOIC representation. It models abstract 'messages' and 'segments' without encoding the mandatory EDIFACT qualifier semantics (NAD+BY vs NAD+SU, DTM+137 vs DTM+35, etc.). Coverage is approximately 15% - only 2 of ~18 required D96A INVOIC segment types are partially modeled, with critical omissions including monetary amounts (MOA), quantities (QTY), dates (DTM), references (RFF), item details (IMD), allowances (ALC), and tax details (TAX).",

  "completeness_score": 0.15,

  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "DTMSegment with qualifier subclasses (DTM+137 DocumentDate, DTM+35 DeliveryDate, DTM+11 DespatchDate)",
      "priority", "owl_reviewed_length": 16959, "consultation_logged": true, "audits_remaining": 0}

